WEBVTT

00:00:01.270 --> 00:00:04.520
October 24th, Torqyean Calendar Year 75.

00:00:04.690 --> 00:00:06.110
The Republic of Venedik

00:00:06.270 --> 00:00:09.980
signed a peace treaty
with the Balt-Rhein Empire,

00:00:10.190 --> 00:00:12.490
with provisions covering
the release of prisoners,

00:00:12.650 --> 00:00:16.410
as well as the trade of Tharrosanwheat.

00:00:16.990 --> 00:00:19.790
It was only three days later that an Imperial ship

00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:26.920
carrying wheat to Phoinike
was sunk by a pirate attack.

00:00:27.130 --> 00:00:29.920
Damn it. This is why I hate the ocean.

00:00:30.130 --> 00:00:32.050
Do you think Minister Louis will be mad?

00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:35.430
There's no way I'm letting him
hold me responsible for this.

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:39.720
Venete Bay is well known for being pirate territory.

00:00:40.470 --> 00:00:45.060
And it just so happens that there
isn't a single Venedician patrol ship today.

00:00:45.190 --> 00:00:50.820
It means we've finally made an enemy
of the Queen of the Centro.

00:00:51.030 --> 00:00:52.900
Good, I'm glad.

00:00:53.150 --> 00:00:57.160
That means the fight has already begun.

00:00:57.320 --> 00:00:59.870
This war began

00:01:00.030 --> 00:01:04.370
when the Empire ignored the rules of the Centro,
and demanded the wheat from us.

00:01:04.830 --> 00:01:10.170
If they mean to subject the Centro
with their policy of "might makes right,"

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:14.050
then we must answer in kind
and ask them to leave by force.

00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:15.380
Yes, Doge,

00:01:16.050 --> 00:01:19.220
but the one we should be fearing
is Torqye's Mahmut Pasha.

00:01:19.430 --> 00:01:20.600
I concur.

00:01:20.850 --> 00:01:24.980
The Empire should have been
an attractive market for us.

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:27.810
If nature was to take its course,

00:01:27.980 --> 00:01:32.230
it should have been years before our interests
would be at odds with the Empire's.

00:01:32.730 --> 00:01:36.400
Mahmut Pasha sped up the clock of history,

00:01:36.570 --> 00:01:41.620
to synchronize the time when our nations
would clash with the Empire.

00:01:42.160 --> 00:01:43.750
It was magnificently done,

00:01:43.910 --> 00:01:45.250
Minister of Foreign Affairs,

00:01:45.410 --> 00:01:48.000
Tughril Mahmut Pasha.

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:52.800
There's so many furs.

00:01:52.960 --> 00:01:56.130
Niki, you should buy a few good ones as well.

00:01:57.340 --> 00:01:59.010
We are heading north.

00:02:06.020 --> 00:02:12.980
Altair: A Record of Battles

00:03:29.930 --> 00:03:33.270
The Northern Kingdom

00:03:33.520 --> 00:03:35.860
It's so incredibly cold.

00:03:36.020 --> 00:03:37.070
November 7th, Torqyean Calendar Year 75.

00:03:37.280 --> 00:03:39.650
Wow, there's a castle coming out of the mountain.

00:03:39.820 --> 00:03:41.150
Those are checkpoints.

00:03:41.740 --> 00:03:43.280
Beyond that is--

00:03:43.530 --> 00:03:45.160
The only nation in this region

00:03:45.370 --> 00:03:48.200
that has remained closed off
since its founding 400 years ago,

00:03:48.410 --> 00:03:50.540
Regatul Urado.

00:03:51.710 --> 00:03:54.130
Our entrance permits and identification papers.

00:03:54.290 --> 00:03:56.840
I believe your minister was contacted about our visit.

00:03:58.300 --> 00:04:01.170
Please, wait! I truly just lost the permit!

00:04:01.340 --> 00:04:04.640
I've been crossing back and forth
for decades to collect firewood!

00:04:04.800 --> 00:04:06.800
Why am I being deported now?!

00:04:06.970 --> 00:04:09.470
My family is waiting for me!

00:04:09.680 --> 00:04:13.560
There isn't a country on this continent
with tougher immigration laws.

00:04:13.730 --> 00:04:15.440
Open the gate!

00:04:16.020 --> 00:04:17.940
Come inside.

00:04:26.530 --> 00:04:30.040
Turn around, and place both hands on the wall.

00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:32.500
Spread your legs.

00:04:35.630 --> 00:04:39.000
-He's clear of infectious disease as well.
-Very good.

00:04:39.500 --> 00:04:41.800
Wait here for the time being.

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:44.430
-What more can you need?
-We still have not

00:04:44.590 --> 00:04:47.300
received word from the minister you've requested.

00:04:47.930 --> 00:04:50.010
An envoy from Torqye, eh?

00:04:50.180 --> 00:04:55.560
You would be a state guest if true,
but a criminal if it's a lie.

00:04:55.730 --> 00:04:58.900
So this is what a closed-off nation is like.

00:05:00.530 --> 00:05:04.780
Excuse me, is Mahmut Pasha here?

00:05:04.990 --> 00:05:06.410
Lady Margit.

00:05:06.610 --> 00:05:08.740
I'm sorry, I was delayed by the snow.

00:05:08.950 --> 00:05:12.950
Mahmut Pasha, allow me
to show you to our capital.

00:05:13.790 --> 00:05:16.080
Forgive us, we did not mean to offend.

00:05:16.330 --> 00:05:21.380
Pardon me for my late introduction.
I am Margit, Diplomatic Minister to Torqye.

00:05:21.550 --> 00:05:23.170
Minister?

00:05:23.380 --> 00:05:26.090
-To the Torqye Pashalu?
-Yes.

00:05:26.550 --> 00:05:28.890
Information on the surrounding nations is vital.

00:05:29.220 --> 00:05:32.890
In my country, a minister is assigned
to each nation,

00:05:33.100 --> 00:05:36.140
and is the point of contact for negotiations.

00:05:37.190 --> 00:05:42.320
Mahmut Pasha, I have heard
much about you from Suleyman Bey.

00:05:43.400 --> 00:05:45.110
I am a kulak.

00:05:45.360 --> 00:05:46.990
A minister being a kulak?

00:05:47.150 --> 00:05:51.080
I had no idea he managed
to recruit someone so important.

00:05:51.240 --> 00:05:54.540
Suleyman Bey is an impressive man.

00:05:54.950 --> 00:06:00.790
Isn't it wonderful to be able to speak directly
with the Chief of Torqye's spy network?

00:06:01.250 --> 00:06:04.840
-Man, that guy really gets the ladies.
-Now, now, Kiros.

00:06:06.050 --> 00:06:09.840
His Majesty is aware that I am a kulak.

00:06:10.090 --> 00:06:15.180
He allows me to gather intelligence
however I see fit.

00:06:15.680 --> 00:06:18.980
I'm sure the ministers in charge
of the Rumerianan nations

00:06:19.150 --> 00:06:23.270
have been quite busy these last few months.

00:06:24.030 --> 00:06:28.320
Could it be that we have arrived too late?

00:06:28.740 --> 00:06:32.990
I'm sorry, I am only informed about
my assigned country.

00:06:35.160 --> 00:06:36.290
What is it?

00:06:40.080 --> 00:06:42.420
They are our lance cavalry, Urado's pride and joy.

00:06:43.170 --> 00:06:45.710
Our country employs a national conscription,

00:06:45.920 --> 00:06:49.510
so we undergo training during the off season
to prepare for emergencies.

00:06:52.300 --> 00:06:54.600
Very impressive. They are quite skilled.

00:06:54.890 --> 00:06:57.060
-Hey, Minister.
-Yes?

00:06:57.220 --> 00:07:00.190
This country was closed off for 400 years, wasn't it?

00:07:00.350 --> 00:07:02.610
Yet you seem well-equipped.

00:07:02.900 --> 00:07:05.570
That means you've provided

00:07:05.780 --> 00:07:09.780
those horses, armor, shields, and lances
all yourself, doesn't it?

00:07:10.030 --> 00:07:13.280
Our nation may be modest, but we have veins of ore,

00:07:13.490 --> 00:07:15.700
as well as the land to raise horses.

00:07:15.910 --> 00:07:17.330
Farmland may be scarce,

00:07:17.540 --> 00:07:23.080
but we have enough resources
to maintain our survival.

00:07:25.090 --> 00:07:27.590
-Is that Iskandar?
-No.

00:07:27.920 --> 00:07:31.220
-That's a northern goshawk.
-Father.

00:07:36.560 --> 00:07:37.850
This is so unexpected.

00:07:38.020 --> 00:07:40.060
I am surprised to see you here.

00:07:42.310 --> 00:07:43.650
Diplomatic Minister.

00:07:43.900 --> 00:07:47.320
That is no way to address me in public.

00:07:48.570 --> 00:07:50.360
My apologies.

00:07:53.030 --> 00:07:55.240
I am sorry you had to see that.

00:07:55.410 --> 00:07:59.450
She is Regatul Urado's fourth princess,
in other words, my daughter.

00:07:59.620 --> 00:08:02.330
Her lack of awareness
about her ministership has been an issue.

00:08:02.540 --> 00:08:05.540
-She's a minister, a kulak, and--
-A princess?

00:08:05.750 --> 00:08:07.960
Then you must be....

00:08:08.380 --> 00:08:11.050
Zygmunt III, King of Urado.

00:08:11.590 --> 00:08:14.640
It has been five years
since a foreign falconer was here last.

00:08:14.800 --> 00:08:18.260
I would be honored if you would
indulge me with a contest.

00:08:24.230 --> 00:08:25.860
Go, Erujebeto.

00:08:27.230 --> 00:08:31.320
The female northern goshawk, the most
dexterous flier among the birds of prey.

00:08:46.290 --> 00:08:51.260
Northern goshawks are best suited
for these hunting grounds,

00:08:51.420 --> 00:08:54.510
surrounded by rocky mountains and trees.

00:08:54.760 --> 00:08:58.300
Perhaps your golden eagle
is at a disadvantage in this contest.

00:08:58.510 --> 00:09:00.100
No, Your Majesty.

00:09:00.260 --> 00:09:02.310
I see a path to victory.

00:09:02.520 --> 00:09:04.600
Really? Show me, then.

00:09:05.020 --> 00:09:06.940
Very well.

00:09:07.350 --> 00:09:08.730
Climb, Iskandar.

00:09:10.900 --> 00:09:13.320
Just as northern goshawks are adept at circling,

00:09:13.530 --> 00:09:15.950
golden eagles are adept at gliding.

00:09:19.410 --> 00:09:21.620
Lying in the north of West Rumeriana,

00:09:21.830 --> 00:09:25.370
sharing borders with
both Torqye and Balt-Rhein is Regatul Urado.

00:09:27.290 --> 00:09:29.790
If Torqye can ally ourselves with this kingdom,

00:09:30.340 --> 00:09:31.590
combined with Venedik,

00:09:31.750 --> 00:09:35.720
half of west Rumeriana will be against the Empire.

00:09:36.680 --> 00:09:42.890
If that happens, even the Empire will have
to reconsider its expansion efforts.

00:09:43.180 --> 00:09:45.890
Very impressive, Tughril Pasha.

00:09:46.100 --> 00:09:48.190
It was quite enjoyable, Your Majesty.

00:09:48.440 --> 00:09:49.730
It may be a poor country,

00:09:49.900 --> 00:09:51.860
with nothing much to show for,

00:09:52.360 --> 00:09:54.860
but you are free to stay as long as you like.

00:09:55.860 --> 00:09:57.610
You have my thanks.

00:09:57.820 --> 00:09:59.780
Minister, I leave them in your hands.

00:09:59.950 --> 00:10:03.200
Yes, understood, Your Majesty.

00:10:03.410 --> 00:10:06.460
Pasha, allow me to speak candidly.

00:10:06.660 --> 00:10:10.170
You will not be able to achieve
your goal in this country.

00:10:10.500 --> 00:10:12.670
Our kingdom has survived on our own

00:10:12.840 --> 00:10:15.460
without any help from other nations
since our founding.

00:10:15.630 --> 00:10:19.510
That is something we wear with pride.

00:10:22.720 --> 00:10:24.100
What's that light?

00:10:24.430 --> 00:10:25.980
This is a fishing village.

00:10:26.140 --> 00:10:29.230
This is just the time the fishermen return home.

00:10:29.440 --> 00:10:32.310
-It's beautiful.
-Yeah.

00:10:33.270 --> 00:10:36.490
What's that strange smell?

00:10:36.690 --> 00:10:39.410
-That really smells.
-You're right.

00:10:39.660 --> 00:10:41.320
What is this smell?

00:10:41.490 --> 00:10:44.410
The smell is coming from those cliffs.

00:10:44.620 --> 00:10:48.870
There is a long stretch of cliffs
west of there that emits a foul odor

00:10:49.080 --> 00:10:51.580
that extends all the way to the border
with the Empire,

00:10:51.750 --> 00:10:53.880
keeping most people away.

00:10:54.920 --> 00:10:56.880
Can't really blame them.

00:10:58.470 --> 00:10:59.880
There's someone there.

00:11:01.550 --> 00:11:05.470
That old man's going
in the opposite direction from the village.

00:11:05.680 --> 00:11:08.230
All right, fine.

00:11:08.430 --> 00:11:11.850
Hey, old man. You're going the wrong way.
The village is that way.

00:11:12.060 --> 00:11:16.860
You're from the fishing village, right?
We'll give you a ride. Hey.

00:11:19.280 --> 00:11:21.160
-Father.
-Thank goodness.

00:11:21.320 --> 00:11:23.570
-Thank you so much.
-Thank you all.

00:11:23.780 --> 00:11:25.200
I'm glad we could help.

00:11:25.370 --> 00:11:27.540
Be more careful next time, old man.

00:11:27.750 --> 00:11:31.120
How could you leave without telling me?

00:11:38.590 --> 00:11:42.050
That old man was planning to die.

00:11:42.220 --> 00:11:45.050
-What?
-This year saw a poor wheat harvest,

00:11:45.260 --> 00:11:48.350
as well as a poor catch from the fishing.
In those times,

00:11:48.720 --> 00:11:51.730
the elderly journey out to the snow fields alone,

00:11:51.940 --> 00:11:55.110
to leave more food for those who remain.

00:11:55.900 --> 00:11:58.980
That family won't likely make it through winter.

00:11:59.240 --> 00:12:01.990
It could be tomorrow, or in two days,
or maybe in ten days,

00:12:02.320 --> 00:12:05.160
but the old man will do the same thing again.

00:12:05.370 --> 00:12:08.240
What, are you serious? This is your country, isn't it?

00:12:08.410 --> 00:12:09.580
Do something.

00:12:09.750 --> 00:12:12.830
If you have enough to dress fancy and feast--

00:12:13.040 --> 00:12:17.290
It is normal in nature that those
who have lost the strength to survive die.

00:12:19.000 --> 00:12:21.840
My father, my grandfather, and great-grandfather

00:12:22.010 --> 00:12:24.340
all died the same way in the snow field.

00:12:24.510 --> 00:12:27.550
I will likely meet a similar end.

00:12:29.010 --> 00:12:32.180
But, Your Majesty, if this is the condition
your kingdom is in,

00:12:32.390 --> 00:12:34.480
why continue with the national isolation?

00:12:34.690 --> 00:12:36.400
If you traded with your neighbors,

00:12:36.560 --> 00:12:39.280
your kingdom should at least be
better off than it is now.

00:12:40.150 --> 00:12:41.240
Pasha,

00:12:41.400 --> 00:12:46.160
Ancient Phoinike went into decline
when it focused on trading with its allies.

00:12:46.370 --> 00:12:49.490
They wasted funds to keep the long
and extensive borders defended,

00:12:49.660 --> 00:12:51.700
and lost national power.

00:12:52.620 --> 00:12:55.120
This fact has been taught for 400 years,

00:12:55.290 --> 00:13:00.460
since the nation of Urado was first founded.

00:13:02.010 --> 00:13:04.590
To avoid the mistakes
of the Ancient Phoinikian Empire,

00:13:05.050 --> 00:13:07.850
Regatul Urado has never tried to expand its territory,

00:13:08.010 --> 00:13:12.430
and never formed allies or trade partners.

00:13:13.560 --> 00:13:15.270
This way.

00:13:16.560 --> 00:13:18.230
Urado is poor.

00:13:18.400 --> 00:13:22.070
As the years come and go,
our forests diminish, and our lands starve.

00:13:22.280 --> 00:13:24.110
We no longer have the strength

00:13:24.280 --> 00:13:27.360
to fight off the coming calamity.

00:13:27.660 --> 00:13:29.530
As a king who threw away his pride

00:13:29.700 --> 00:13:31.410
and broke 400 years of conviction,

00:13:31.580 --> 00:13:34.370
-I am prepared to take the blame.
-Father.

00:13:34.830 --> 00:13:38.250
There is still hope for Urado.

00:13:38.420 --> 00:13:40.290
Margit.

00:13:40.460 --> 00:13:45.840
Your Majesty, we have just received
an official new offer from the nation.

00:13:45.970 --> 00:13:47.090
Sister.

00:13:47.300 --> 00:13:52.510
Thanks to our negotiations,
it offers plenty of benefit to us.

00:13:53.640 --> 00:13:57.350
All that's needed is your approval.

00:13:57.560 --> 00:13:59.730
Torqye was too late.

00:13:59.900 --> 00:14:01.070
No.

00:14:04.280 --> 00:14:08.280
I don't like any of this.

00:14:09.160 --> 00:14:12.120
That smell got in.

00:14:13.160 --> 00:14:16.080
That's it. I remember what smell this is.

00:14:17.080 --> 00:14:20.580
That's the smell of the sterco
found on the Centro's Sudd Island.

00:14:20.790 --> 00:14:21.880
Sterco?

00:14:22.040 --> 00:14:23.380
What do you say?

00:14:23.590 --> 00:14:28.340
Shall we ask Minister Margit if we can
check out those cliffs?

00:14:29.090 --> 00:14:31.010
You want to go now?

00:14:37.230 --> 00:14:39.810
Okay, keep it steady.

00:14:40.350 --> 00:14:44.730
The stench is strong, but it doesn't seem
to be the nesting grounds of seabirds.

00:14:45.230 --> 00:14:47.820
Good Lord, that smells so bad.

00:14:51.030 --> 00:14:54.620
Remnants of fish that's been eaten,
and bird footprints.

00:14:54.910 --> 00:14:56.370
This looks to be quite old.

00:14:56.540 --> 00:14:58.870
This is called Bird Beach,

00:14:59.080 --> 00:15:02.880
and was once the nesting grounds
of millions of seabirds.

00:15:03.170 --> 00:15:05.750
They were also a valuable food source
for the villagers.

00:15:05.920 --> 00:15:10.050
So in 400 years, they ate every single last one?

00:15:10.260 --> 00:15:12.340
Wait, so this smell is--

00:15:12.510 --> 00:15:15.060
The smell of seabird droppings.

00:15:17.020 --> 00:15:20.640
Stercos are fossilized feces that were
formed by the bird droppings.

00:15:20.810 --> 00:15:26.610
It's said that the entirety of the Centro's Sudd Island
was made up of sterco.

00:15:26.820 --> 00:15:31.320
-I'm in hell.
-No, it's heaven, in some sense.

00:15:31.490 --> 00:15:35.030
-For here, too, if this is really sterco.
-What do you mean?

00:15:35.490 --> 00:15:38.700
Padrone, I would like your help with something.

00:15:44.380 --> 00:15:48.050
Oh, God, that smells. As far as harassment goes,

00:15:48.210 --> 00:15:50.130
it can't get much worse.

00:15:50.300 --> 00:15:51.380
Not since the inquiry.

00:15:51.880 --> 00:15:54.890
-Who is it from?
-Mahmut Pasha.

00:15:55.970 --> 00:15:58.640
Really? What is it?

00:15:58.930 --> 00:16:01.640
Sterco extracted from Bird Beach.

00:16:01.810 --> 00:16:03.940
If these sea sparkles react the same way,

00:16:04.270 --> 00:16:07.440
then it's identical to the sterco from Sudd Island.

00:16:07.730 --> 00:16:08.940
Sterco?

00:16:09.490 --> 00:16:12.110
I'm surprised it still exists.

00:16:12.320 --> 00:16:15.410
This should be the last of it all.

00:16:15.570 --> 00:16:19.410
I guess that's why you're examining it yourself.

00:16:19.620 --> 00:16:21.210
It's for Torqye.

00:16:21.370 --> 00:16:24.370
If this is something that can help us fight the Empire,

00:16:24.830 --> 00:16:26.750
I can't entrust it to someone else.

00:16:26.920 --> 00:16:28.960
If you say so.

00:16:29.300 --> 00:16:30.380
It's glowing.

00:16:32.340 --> 00:16:34.380
Wow, this is...

00:16:34.590 --> 00:16:37.510
Of higher quality than the sterco from Sudd Island.

00:16:37.800 --> 00:16:40.470
Thank you. Take care.

00:16:44.230 --> 00:16:46.520
Thank you, Zaganos Pasha.

00:16:46.690 --> 00:16:49.270
Now Urado can escape poverty.

00:16:51.110 --> 00:16:55.110
-What are you doing, barging in here so late?
-His Majesty requires your presence.

00:16:55.280 --> 00:16:59.450
Once you get dressed,
come to the northern hall immediately.

00:17:03.160 --> 00:17:06.540
Please, step forward, Mahmut Pasha.

00:17:17.800 --> 00:17:20.060
Someone's there?

00:17:20.470 --> 00:17:23.430
The king will announce his decision presently.

00:17:24.140 --> 00:17:28.020
As of the signing of this treaty,
Regatul Urado will enter the protection

00:17:28.190 --> 00:17:30.440
of the Balt-Rhein Empire.

00:17:30.940 --> 00:17:32.440
What?

00:17:32.690 --> 00:17:35.530
Your decisive judgment is appreciated, Your Majesty.

00:17:35.820 --> 00:17:39.910
Our Empire shall do its utmost
to reward your wise decision.

00:17:42.200 --> 00:17:46.000
An Imperial envoy. So they did have the initiative.

00:17:46.290 --> 00:17:50.710
Your Majesty, in exchange for allowing
our Imperial forces free entry to your country,

00:17:50.880 --> 00:17:54.720
the Urado royal family shall maintain its sovereignty.

00:17:54.880 --> 00:17:58.300
We shall deliver our promise
of providing food and necessities,

00:17:58.510 --> 00:18:03.680
as well as sharing our technology and knowledge.

00:18:04.140 --> 00:18:06.390
This country has reached its life span.

00:18:06.560 --> 00:18:10.310
However, its citizens must continue to live.

00:18:11.440 --> 00:18:15.530
The king said I would not be able
to achieve my goals.

00:18:15.690 --> 00:18:18.320
Then why did he bother summoning us here now?

00:18:19.280 --> 00:18:21.410
Is it because he is hoping for another option,

00:18:21.580 --> 00:18:25.870
despite making such a declaration?

00:18:26.160 --> 00:18:30.330
Your Majesty, this country has
not yet reached its life span.

00:18:31.750 --> 00:18:34.960
You are familiar with the uninhabited coastline
that emits a foul odor

00:18:35.130 --> 00:18:37.130
in the northern Urado territories?

00:18:37.510 --> 00:18:42.100
There was an isolated island in the Centro
that gave off an identical stench.

00:18:42.300 --> 00:18:43.850
Its name is Sudd Island,

00:18:44.010 --> 00:18:47.600
an island that yielded excellent fertilizer
hailed as a miracle.

00:18:47.850 --> 00:18:51.020
The fertilizer was sold to agricultural nations

00:18:51.190 --> 00:18:53.860
for high sums of money,
with demand never waning.

00:18:54.440 --> 00:18:58.360
However, it was completely depleted
50 years ago.

00:18:58.860 --> 00:19:00.610
The fertilizer's name was sterco,

00:19:00.820 --> 00:19:03.870
and it is made from fossilized sea bird droppings.

00:19:04.660 --> 00:19:09.460
That same substance is covering Bird Beach.

00:19:09.670 --> 00:19:12.500
If you export this sterco to the eastern nations,

00:19:12.960 --> 00:19:15.300
there is no telling the amount of wealth
you could bring in.

00:19:16.960 --> 00:19:19.680
The Torqye Pashalu shall arrange for the caravans

00:19:19.840 --> 00:19:21.890
and secure the trade route to the East.

00:19:22.510 --> 00:19:27.930
If you join forces with us, I promise
we can revitalize Regatul Urado together.

00:19:28.100 --> 00:19:32.520
That arrangement may sound beneficial for Urado,

00:19:32.650 --> 00:19:36.530
but wouldn't Torqye simply be using
Urado's inexperience with commerce

00:19:36.690 --> 00:19:39.280
to reap all the benefits?

00:19:40.150 --> 00:19:42.530
That is not true!

00:19:43.570 --> 00:19:45.410
Margit.

00:19:46.700 --> 00:19:49.370
Our country is ill.

00:19:49.620 --> 00:19:53.750
Entering the Empire's protection
would not cure our disease.

00:19:53.920 --> 00:19:55.840
They will bind string around our body,

00:19:56.000 --> 00:19:58.880
and make it impossible
to survive without their support.

00:19:59.260 --> 00:20:04.140
But forming an alliance with Torqye
will allow us to cure our ailment,

00:20:04.340 --> 00:20:07.680
and give us the ability
to stand on our two feet again.

00:20:08.060 --> 00:20:10.980
Joining with Torqye is in the best interests
of our country.

00:20:11.140 --> 00:20:14.270
-Do not be so stupid, Margit.
-Sister.

00:20:14.520 --> 00:20:17.610
Rumeriana is preparing for war.

00:20:17.770 --> 00:20:20.820
What's vital is to join the more powerful side.

00:20:20.990 --> 00:20:24.530
It's foolish to make an enemy out of
a major military power like Balt-Rhein

00:20:24.700 --> 00:20:26.530
just because they found some fertilizer.

00:20:26.830 --> 00:20:31.040
Very astute observation, Lady Gerutorudo.

00:20:31.200 --> 00:20:35.000
But worry not, as long as you are with the Empire,

00:20:35.170 --> 00:20:37.040
we shall guarantee Urado's prosperity.

00:20:37.250 --> 00:20:41.050
You also expect them to be the first troops
leading the charge in your invasion.

00:20:42.170 --> 00:20:47.100
A nation becomes the very thing
most suited to its environment.

00:20:47.760 --> 00:20:50.560
Just as Urado was able to impose
their isolationist policies

00:20:50.720 --> 00:20:53.350
because of their location
that afforded self-sufficiency,

00:20:53.520 --> 00:20:55.900
Venedik, where only salt and fish are available,

00:20:56.100 --> 00:20:58.690
turned to trade and commerce.

00:20:58.860 --> 00:21:00.820
And the major military power Balt-Rhein,

00:21:00.980 --> 00:21:04.200
whose livelihood is based on
agriculture and livestock, values land,

00:21:04.360 --> 00:21:06.780
which destines it for aggression.

00:21:07.740 --> 00:21:11.450
Your Majesty, I am sure you are familiar
with the Empire's invasion of Phoinike,

00:21:11.620 --> 00:21:13.870
and the vassalization of Tharros,

00:21:14.500 --> 00:21:18.960
and how these people are being treated.

00:21:19.130 --> 00:21:21.000
In order to avoid repeating their tragedy,

00:21:21.170 --> 00:21:24.590
we must unite all the nations of the Centro together.

00:21:25.090 --> 00:21:28.890
If Balt-Rhein's prosperity
is dependent on invasion,

00:21:29.100 --> 00:21:32.930
then the prosperity of the nations of commerce
is dependent on peace.

00:21:33.480 --> 00:21:35.850
Do you become the advance guard for invasion,

00:21:36.060 --> 00:21:40.480
or join Torqye to stop the war
trying to break out across the continent?

00:21:40.730 --> 00:21:44.490
Which do you choose, Your Majesty?

00:21:46.570 --> 00:21:48.870
Take the Imperial Envoy to the execution grounds.

00:21:49.370 --> 00:21:52.040
What? Please wait, Your Majesty.

00:21:52.240 --> 00:21:54.540
This is not what we agreed upon.

00:21:54.750 --> 00:21:59.290
Do you know what this means?
If I don't return to the Empire--

00:22:00.250 --> 00:22:03.380
Our kingdom shall join forces with Torqye.

00:22:03.670 --> 00:22:09.930
I vow that we will never join sides with Balt-Rhein.

00:22:12.930 --> 00:22:17.060
I will do my utmost to
honor the trust you have put in us.

00:23:48.280 --> 00:23:52.530
Does that mean we got saved
from execution by bird droppings?

00:23:52.780 --> 00:23:57.040
Let's leave this freezing country behind already,
and get back home to Torqye.

00:23:57.240 --> 00:23:59.540
Next time, "Beginning of the Great War."

00:23:59.750 --> 00:24:02.420
What's that sly fox doing here?
